<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="unit1-summary">
  <title>Unit 1 Summary</title>

  <p>In Unit 1, we covered the following Learning Objectives:</p>
   <ul>
    <li><p>1.1 Purpose and Behavior
    <ul>
      <li>1.1.A Determine the purpose and behavior of an app by interacting with it.</li>
      <li>1.1.B Identify inputs and outputs of an app while using it.</li>
    </ul>
    </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.2 Benefits of Collaboration
    <ul>
      <li>1.2.A Explain how apps and programs are improved through collaboration and user testing.</li>
      <li>1.2.B Explain how collaboration can reduce bias in apps.</li>
    </ul></p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.3 Responsible AI and Human Decision-Making
    <ul>
      <li>1.3.A Explain how human decisions shape the development, deployment, and maintenance of AI tools.</li>
      <li>1.3.B Evaluate the appropriate level of automation or augmentation for a task.</li>
    </ul></p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.4 Binary Representation
    <ul>
      <li>1.4.A Explain how computers store and process data as bits, and how those bits are represented as meaningful digital information for users.</li>
      <li>1.4.B Explain why representing numbers with limited bits can produce inaccurate results.</li>
    </ul></p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.5 Sequencing
    <ul>
      <li>1.5.A Represent an algorithm that uses sequencing using written steps or a flowchart.</li>
      <li>1.5.B Develop code that runs sequentially, and determine the result of sequential statements.</li>
    </ul></p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.6 Variables
    <ul>
      <li>1.6.A Identify the use of variables in an app while interacting with it.</li>
      <li>1.6.B Develop code for assignment statements using variables, and determine the values that are stored in the variables as a result.</li>
      <li>1.6.C Develop code to store and modify strings, and determine the output produced.</li>
    </ul></p>
    </li>
    <li><p>1.7 Mathematical Expressions
    <ul>
      <li>1.7.A Develop code using mathematical expressions, and determine the result of these expressions.</li>
      <li>1.7.B Develop code to generate random numbers, and determine the possible values that could be produced as a result.</li>
   </ul></p>
   </li>
 </ul>

  <p>Review the following Unit 1 vocabulary:</p>

   <activity label="vocab-IO-review">
      <statement>
        <p>
          1-1 Purpose and Behavior Vocabulary. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it
          on its correct definition on the right.
          Click the "Check Me" button to see if you are correct.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <feedback>
        <p>Review the vocabulary in 1.1and try again.</p>
      </feedback>

      <cardsort>
        <match>
          <premise>app</premise>
          <response>a program that runs on a computer or any computing device</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>purpose</premise>
          <response>why an app exists or its goal</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>behavior</premise>
          <response>what an app does when used</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>input</premise>
          <response>data sent to a computer for a program to process.</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>output</premise>
          <response>data sent back from a program to the device or user</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>user interface (UI)</premise>
          <response>the part of an app (for example buttons) that users directly interact with</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>event</premise>
          <response>a signal that something happened, such as a button click or key press</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>event handler</premise>
          <response>code that runs in response to an event</response>
        </match>
      </cardsort>
    </activity>

    <activity label="binary-vocab-review">
      <statement>
        <p>
          1-4 Binary Vocabulary. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it
          on its correct definition on the right.
          Click the "Check Me" button to see if you are correct.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <feedback>
        <p>Find the words in 1-4 and try again.</p>
      </feedback>

      <cardsort>
        <match>
          <premise order="1">bit</premise>
          <response>A binary digit, either 0 or 1.</response>
        </match>

        <match>
          <premise order="2">abstraction</premise>
          <response>The process of removing detail to focus on the essential characteristics of
            something.</response>
        </match>

        <match>
          <premise order="3">encoding</premise>
          <response>Converting information into a specific format for storage or transmission.</response>
        </match>

        <match>
          <premise order="4">roundoff error</premise>
          <response>The error that occurs when a number is approximated to fit in a fixed number of
            bits.</response>
        </match>

        <match>
          <premise order="5">overflow error</premise>
          <response>The error that occurs when a number is too large to be represented within the
            given number of bits.</response>
        </match>
      </cardsort>
    </activity>

      <activity label="sequencing-vocab-review">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Review the vocabulary in 1-5 Sequencing. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it
          on its correct definition on the right.
          Click the "Check Me" button to see if you are correct.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <feedback>
        <p>Find the words in 1-5 above and try again.</p>
      </feedback>

      <cardsort>
        <match>
          <premise order="1">algorithm</premise>
          <response>Step by step instructions for solving a problem</response>
        </match>
        <match>
        <premise order="8">sequencing</premise>
        <response>The default order of code that is run line-by-line from the top down</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise order="2">flowchart</premise>
          <response>Visual representation of an algorithm that uses shapes and arrows to show the steps</response>
        </match>

        <match>
          <premise order="3">IDE</premise>
          <response>Software that provides tools for programmers to write, test, and debug code</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise order="5">syntax error</premise>
          <response>A mistake in the way code is written that prevents it from running correctly</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise order="6">debugging</premise>
          <response>The process of finding and fixing errors in code</response>
        </match>  
      </cardsort>
    </activity>

        <activity label="vars-vocab-review">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Review the vocabulary in 1-6 Variables. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it
          on its correct definition on the right.
          Click the "Check Me" button to see if you are correct.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <feedback>
        <p>Find the words in 1-6 and try again.</p>
      </feedback>

      <cardsort>
        <match>
        <premise>variable</premise>
        <response>a named storage location used to hold a value that can change
        while the program is running</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>program state</premise>
          <response>the set of values and information a program is storing at a specific
        moment</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>data types</premise>
          <response>numbers, strings, or booleans</response>
        </match>
        <match>
          <premise>string</premise>
          <response>an ordered sequence of characters used to represent text in a
        program</response>
        </match>
         <match>
          <premise>concatenation</premise>
          <response>joins two or more strings to create a new string</response>
        </match>
         <match>
          <premise>substring</premise>
          <response>part of an existing string</response>
        </match>
  </cardsort>
  </activity>
    <activity label="vocab-exprs-review">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Review the vocabulary in 1-7 Expressions. Drag the vocabulary term from the left and drop it
          on its correct definition on the right.
          Click the "Check Me" button to see if you are correct.
        </p>
      </statement>

      <feedback>
        <p>Find the words in 1-7 and try again.</p>
